  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Risk of isolated strong storms on the decrease\novernight.\n\nLate evening update. Updated the HWO, chance of any strong\nstorms about over with.\n\nMore information below.\n\nMid evening update.\n\nSPC did cut back on the oulk. As was the case around 5 PM\nyesterday and today, strong to severe storms formed just to our\nnorth and east, near the front. \n\nStill a few strong storms just to our north, but expect this \nactivity to remain mainly outside our area. Temperatures across \nthe north not all that warm now.\n\nFurther to the southeast, just to the northeast of MDT, a few\ncells formed in the warmer and more humid airmass, but the\nhighest dewpoints mainly near the river, and given trends and\ntime of day, hard to see much going on with these cells. \n\nActivity to the northwest has been weakening.\n\nTemperatures on track for the overnight period. \n\nMore information below.\n\nMeso models continue to display a fairly wide spread on the\nconvective evolution through tonight. In general, we're favoring\nin increase in precip potential from NNW to SSE (downstream of\nLake Erie and ongoing tstm activity in southern Ontario/western\nNY) from later this afternoon into the early overnight hours.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Brief break from the episodic precip pattern and\nhigh humidity into the weekend before thunderstorm chances \nreturn Sunday.\n\nLooks like the more active day may be Sunday vs. Monday, but\ncould see the activity linger into Monday. Like recent events,\nwarm advection and directional shear support storm formation, \nas the warm air moves back into the area on Sunday.\n\nMore information below.\n\nLatest trends suggest the front will have a harder time pushing\nsouth of the MD line into the weekend. We still expect a brief\nbreak in the episodic tstm precip pattern and very muggy\nconditions Friday night into Saturday, but the chance of rain \nwill linger over portions of the southern tier of CPA. Ensemble\ndata shows a ramp in precip odds for Sunday into Sunday night in\nadvance of a frontal system pushing eastward from the Great\nLakes and Ohio Valley.",
